Verify the convergence of GMRES. The inner loop stops as soon as the
Arnoldi estimate of the residual meets the tolerance, without ever
computing the residual. With an ill-conditioned preconditioner the
estimate drifts away from the real residual, and GMRES reports
convergence for a wrong solution (SPARSE_mpi_22: 10 iterations, 1% error;
SPARSE_mpi_2: 19 iterations, 24% error). Only leave the outer loop after
the recomputed residual meets the tolerance, otherwise restart.

diff --git a/src/iterative/GMRes.cpp b/src/iterative/GMRes.cpp
index e7fd4962..a0e4a552 100644
--- a/src/iterative/GMRes.cpp
+++ b/src/iterative/GMRes.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,11 @@ namespace strumpack {
                       << "\trel.res = " << std::setw(12)
                       << rho/rho0 << std::endl;
           if ((rho < atol) || (rho/rho0 < rtol) || (totit >= maxit)) {
-            no_conv = false;
+            // rho is only the Arnoldi estimate of the residual, which
+            // drifts from the real one when the preconditioner is
+            // ill-conditioned: update x and let the start of the
+            // outer loop check the recomputed residual
+            if (totit >= maxit) no_conv = false;
             nrit = it;
             break;
           }
